  "articleBody": "Thinking about getting rid of that old tub? A bathroom tub removal project can really open up your space, but a little prep goes a long way. First, you'll want to think about what's replacing it. Is it a walk-in shower, or just more open floor space? This decision impacts the entire project, from plumbing changes to flooring. You should also consider what's happening with the surrounding walls and existing plumbing – sometimes moving a tub means adjusting pipes or patching walls. Disruption is part of any remodel, so mentally prepare for that! Make sure to clear out the bathroom completely; this includes removing all personal items, towels, and anything else you don't want getting dusty or in the way. It’s also wise to cover nearby furniture or doorways to contain dust. A huge mistake folks make is not confirming the demolition scope beforehand, leading to surprises. Make sure you and your contractor are on the same page about what’s being removed and what’s staying. And remember, once the tub is gone, you'll have an exposed area that needs proper waterproofing and finishing. This is where a professional truly shines, ensuring no hidden damage or future leaks. HH Remodeling LLC emphasizes clear communication, so you’ll be informed throughout. Don't underestimate hidden damage or skip planning for plumbing or electrical changes before walls are opened. A professional touch ensures everything is handled correctly. Give HH Remodeling LLC a call to discuss your tub removal project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
